gm-method/rendering (a model renders TINY + rotated-wrong + only-some-tris while its physics collider is CORRECT -- the split is the diagnostic): the collider and the renderer consume the asset through DIFFERENT transform paths, so a transform applied an extra time on ONLY the render path produces exactly this signature (tiny + mis-rotated render, correct collision). Do NOT re-bake/re-convert the source asset on this symptom -- witness first: (1) dump the source AND baked GLB node transforms (a glTF importer puts a single import-scale e.g. 0.03 + an axis-fix rotation e.g. quat[-0.707,0,0,0.707] = -90deg X for Z-up->Y-up on ONE root node, children identity) -- if source==baked the FILE is fine; (2) read the LIVE scene graph chain via a window global (window.__app.modelPool._entities) and decompose each node's world scale down to the leaf -- a leaf whose world scale is the import-scale SQUARED (0.03*0.03=0.0009, model 1792 units rendering as 1.6m instead of 54m) is a DOUBLE-APPLIED node TRS. ROOT CAUSE pattern in a cluster/instanced LOD loader: it does mesh.applyMatrix4(src.matrixWorld) to bake the placement THEN re-parents the new mesh under src.parent -- but src.parent IS the node whose TRS is already folded into src.matrixWorld, so the scale+rotation apply twice. THE FIX (matches the loader's own discrete-LOD path): apply the transform RELATIVE to the entity root (rootInverse x src.matrixWorld) and parent the new mesh under the root (identity scale), never under the scaled source parent. Witness the fix by re-reading the live leaf world scale (0.0009 -> 0.03) and world AABB (1.6m -> ~54m). Lock with a mock-free SOURCE-SHAPE test assertion (the bake test.js cannot render): assert the cluster path text does NOT contain the buggy parent.add(scaledParent) and DOES contain the rootInverse-relative transform -- same idiom as asserting no LOD band left at the implicit-0 form.